<title>PORTUGAL: Bortugal's BCP H1 profit up 21 pct.</title>
<headline>Bortugal's BCP H1 profit up 21 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 22.</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit	   13.12    vs    10.81</p>
<p>    Earnings per share	93.2 esc vs    91.6 esc</p>
<p>    Return on Equity	  13.0 pct vs    12.1 pct</p>
<p>Profit before tax</p>
<p>    and minority interest   31.78    vs    24.25</p>
<p>    Return on assets	   1.0 pct vs     0.8 pct</p>
<p>Note - Banco Comercial Portugues is Portugal's largest non-state bank.  </p>
<p>    Total assets	   5,622.0     vs 5,255.0</p>
<p>    Client funds	   4,990.0     vs 4,256.0</p>
<p>    Client loans	   2,395.0     vs 2,093.0</p>
<p>Unperforming loans</p>
<p>    over 90 days		 3.1 pct vs     4.1</p>
<p>Previsions against</p>
<p>    unperforming loans     108.6 pct vs   103.8</p>
<p>    Solvability ratio	 10.8 pct vs     9.7</p>
<p>The bank said that sustained growth in its financial margins, significant growth in commission income and rising returns on investment, together with a reduction in costs lay behind the 21 percent increase in net profit.</p>
<p>Net commissions rose 39 percent in the first six months, the bank said.</p>
<p>The pace of growth had compensated for the dilution effect on earnings per share of the 150 billion escudo capital increase carried out in April 1996 and May 1997, the bank added.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
